# {{.Name}}

A Caja **http-api** project — `main.caja` uses [`@caja/acerola`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@caja/acerola)
(route groups, table-driven routes, and middleware presets over the `http`
builtin module) to declare routes, and compiles to a native Go binary.

`caja init` installed `@caja/acerola` for you via npm/bun when this project
was created. If that step was skipped (no package manager found, offline, or
`--skip-install` was passed), run `npm install` (or `bun install`, `yarn install`) here
first.

## Running locally

```
caja listen
```

Runs `main.caja` as a live local server. Pass `--port` to override the port
the CLI binds to (independent of the port literal passed to `http.listen`
in the script).

## Building

```
caja build
```

Compiles `main.caja` to a native binary for your platform, which you can run
directly or deploy anywhere that runs Go binaries.
